invariant: INV-22
file: tcp_nonblocking_frame.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: the tcp-nonblocking reader reads an alert in the clear only until its
  read key is installed, so a server that has sent its flight decrypts the
  alert of a client that could not use the ServerHello, fails it with
  bad_record_mac and owes an answer to an alert that closed the connection.
  bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires the server to record the client's
  alert in the clear after its flight and to owe nothing.

--- old
    if (outer == REC_ALERT) {
        r->hs.alert = ALERT_UNEXPECTED_MESSAGE;
--- new
    if (outer == REC_ALERT && !r->hs.encrypted) {
        r->hs.alert = ALERT_UNEXPECTED_MESSAGE;
